  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_022 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) at 0.7250 accuracy, with config_027 (same encoders, avgpool + weighted) at 0.7062. Across all experiments, scvi_n200 and imagenet_vit_l are clearly superior encoders, multiprofile outperforms singleprofile, and transformer aggregation beats avgpool. The only untested variant within this top-performing encoder/aggregation family is concat fusion (config_050: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat). Question: Does concat fusion interact differently with transformer aggregation than it did with avgpool (where weighted consistently beat concat, e.g., config_012 vs config_004)? This is the best use of experiment 9 because it completes the 2×2 fusion×aggregation grid for the best encoder pair, confirming or refuting whether weighted fusion is strictly dominant. If config_050 matches or exceeds 0.725, it becomes the new best; if not, it solidifies config_022 as the final answer for the last experiment. Expected cost: ~3.5–4 GPU hours (same architecture as config_022, only fusion layer differs), well within budget."
}

